{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SeminormalV21Trace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SeminormalV21Trace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma1_mul_sigma2_forces_constant_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma1_mul_sigma2_forces_constant_phase","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**The obstruction, stated.**  `σ₁σ₂` satisfies `det = 1` and has constant\ntrace `−1`; so if it were the transfer matrix, `2 cos α = −1` would force\n`α = 2π/3` — a constant, with no dependence on `q` and in particular not\n`(z−1)h/2`, which is non-constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.det_sigma1_mul_sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.det_sigma1_mul_sigma2","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L125-L130","doc":"`det (σ₁σ₂) = 1`, so `σ₁σ₂` *does* meet the determinant half of\n`TransferMatrixSpectrum` — it is the trace half that fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.trace_sigma1_mul_sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.trace_sigma1_mul_sigma2","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L117-L123","doc":"**`trace (σ₁σ₂) = −1`, identically in `q`.**  The `q`-dependence cancels\nexactly — this is the sharpest instance of the integrality obstruction, and it\npins the eigenphase of `σ₁σ₂` to the constant `2π/3`, not to `(z−1)h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma1_mul_sigma2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma1_mul_sigma2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L109-L115","doc":"The explicit product `σ₁σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.trace_entries_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.trace_entries_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L100-L107","doc":"The scalar content of the trace identity: `q·d₂ − q⁻¹·d₁ = −1`.  The\n`q`-dependence cancels exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.det_sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.det_sigma2","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L92-L98","doc":"`det σ₂ = −1`.  Both generators are unimodular-up-to-sign, which is the\nsource of the parity obstruction: a word of length `L` has determinant `(−1)^L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.det_sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.det_sigma1","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L86-L90","doc":"`det σ₁ = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.bCoupling_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.bCoupling_sq","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L74-L84","doc":"**The off-diagonal square is `d₁d₂ + 1`** — i.e. the determinant condition\n`det σ₂ = −1` is what fixes the Hoefsmit coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.d1_add_d2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.d1_add_d2","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L66-L72","doc":"`d₁ + d₂ = h = q − q⁻¹`: the Hecke trace condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma2","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L62-L64","doc":"`σ₂` in the symmetric gauge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.bCoupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.bCoupling","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L57-L60","doc":"Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling, `b = √(q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1)` — the same constant\nas `QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB`, here in its role as the seminormal off-diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.d2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.d2","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L54-L55","doc":"Upper-left seminormal entry, `d₂ = −1/(q(q²+1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.d1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.d1","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L51-L52","doc":"Lower-right seminormal entry, `d₁ = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Seminormal.sigma1","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeminormalV21Trace.lean#L45-L49","doc":"`σ₁ = diag(q, −q⁻¹)`: on the two standard tableaux of shape `(2,1)`, the\nentries `1` and `2` share a row in the first and a column in the second, giving\nthe Hecke eigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}